1
00:00:00,290 --> 00:00:02,690
If your knee replacement
still hurts

2
00:00:02,690 --> 00:00:05,340
and the X-ray keeps coming
back fine,

3
00:00:05,340 --> 00:00:06,780
don't accept that.

4
00:00:06,780 --> 00:00:07,800
I've been a landscaper

5
00:00:07,800 --> 00:00:09,490
for twenty-nine years.

6
00:00:09,490 --> 00:00:10,460
Kneeling in the dirt,

7
00:00:10,460 --> 00:00:11,810
digging, and pushing mowers

8
00:00:11,810 --> 00:00:12,950
all day long.

9
00:00:12,950 --> 00:00:13,980
I had my right knee

10
00:00:13,980 --> 00:00:15,850
replaced two years ago.

11
00:00:15,850 --> 00:00:18,400
It has hurt every day
since.

12
00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:20,340
Not surgery pain.

13
00:00:20,340 --> 00:00:21,620
I know what that felt
like,

14
00:00:21,620 --> 00:00:22,790
and it went away.

15
00:00:22,790 --> 00:00:23,980
This is different.

16
00:00:23,980 --> 00:00:24,370
Tight.

17
00:00:24,370 --> 00:00:25,320
Full.

18
00:00:25,320 --> 00:00:26,270
Like a band around

19
00:00:26,270 --> 00:00:27,880
the joint that never
loosens.

20
00:00:27,880 --> 00:00:28,730
And for two years

21
00:00:28,730 --> 00:00:30,600
I've been told the same
thing.

22
00:00:30,600 --> 00:00:31,780
Give it time.

23
00:00:31,780 --> 00:00:33,790
At six weeks it was
swelling,

24
00:00:33,790 --> 00:00:35,330
and swelling is normal.

25
00:00:35,330 --> 00:00:36,020
At three months,

26
00:00:36,020 --> 00:00:37,130
give it six.

27
00:00:37,130 --> 00:00:37,840
At six months,

28
00:00:37,840 --> 00:00:39,680
some knees take a full
year.

29
00:00:39,680 --> 00:00:40,160
At a year,

30
00:00:40,160 --> 00:00:41,790
eighteen months isn't
unusual.

31
00:00:41,790 --> 00:00:42,970
And I didn't just wait.

32
00:00:42,970 --> 00:00:44,290
We went down the list.

33
00:00:44,290 --> 00:00:45,870
More physical therapy.

34
00:00:45,870 --> 00:00:46,940
Every session,

35
00:00:46,940 --> 00:00:48,930
every exercise at home.

36
00:00:48,930 --> 00:00:50,330
I got stronger.

37
00:00:50,330 --> 00:00:51,670
The tightness never moved.

38
00:00:51,670 --> 00:00:53,290
The pain pills helped,

39
00:00:53,290 --> 00:00:54,750
and that was the problem.

40
00:00:54,750 --> 00:00:56,770
I'm already on enough
every morning,

41
00:00:56,770 --> 00:00:57,870
and nobody could tell me

42
00:00:57,870 --> 00:00:59,640
when I'd get to stop.

43
00:00:59,640 --> 00:01:01,100
Then a nerve block.

44
00:01:01,100 --> 00:01:03,520
Then talk of burning the
nerve.

45
00:01:03,520 --> 00:01:05,030
And after that, a second

46
00:01:05,030 --> 00:01:06,730
operation to go back

47
00:01:06,730 --> 00:01:08,260
in and do it over.

48
00:01:08,260 --> 00:01:09,790
I said no.

49
00:01:09,790 --> 00:01:12,220
Every morning I pulled
on my work gloves

50
00:01:12,220 --> 00:01:13,380
and my knee felt like

51
00:01:13,380 --> 00:01:15,270
a band was wrapped around
it,

52
00:01:15,270 --> 00:01:17,810
tightening every inch I
tried to straighten.

53
00:01:17,810 --> 00:01:20,180
Every morning I took
something for it

54
00:01:20,180 --> 00:01:21,900
and went to work.

55
00:01:21,900 --> 00:01:23,350
I'd load the trailer,

56
00:01:23,350 --> 00:01:24,490
start the mower,

57
00:01:24,490 --> 00:01:25,830
and grit my teeth through

58
00:01:25,830 --> 00:01:27,500
every yard on the list.

59
00:01:27,500 --> 00:01:28,930
Couldn't do the stairs,

60
00:01:28,930 --> 00:01:30,040
couldn't stand at the
counter

61
00:01:30,040 --> 00:01:31,700
long enough to finish
dinner,

62
00:01:31,700 --> 00:01:32,840
couldn't kneel long enough

63
00:01:32,840 --> 00:01:34,340
to finish a flower bed,

64
00:01:34,340 --> 00:01:35,760
couldn't sit through my
granddaughter's

65
00:01:35,760 --> 00:01:38,370
game without shifting
every two minutes.

66
00:01:38,370 --> 00:01:39,940
It woke me at night,

67
00:01:39,940 --> 00:01:42,000
and it turned ordinary
things,

68
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:43,520
like getting in the car

69
00:01:43,520 --> 00:01:44,820
or up off the couch,

70
00:01:44,820 --> 00:01:46,260
into a decision.

71
00:01:46,260 --> 00:01:47,720
After a long and serious

72
00:01:47,720 --> 00:01:49,020
talk with my wife,

73
00:01:49,020 --> 00:01:51,130
I went back in one more
time.

74
00:01:51,130 --> 00:01:52,470
That was the fourth set

75
00:01:52,470 --> 00:01:54,260
of X-rays on this knee.

76
00:01:54,260 --> 00:01:55,780
And like the three before
it,

77
00:01:55,780 --> 00:01:58,400
the answer was everything
looks great.

78
00:01:58,400 --> 00:02:01,060
No loosening, no
infection,

79
00:02:01,060 --> 00:02:02,590
nothing wrong.

80
00:02:02,590 --> 00:02:03,880
Only this time there

81
00:02:03,880 --> 00:02:05,370
was no new number.

82
00:02:05,370 --> 00:02:06,060
Nobody said

83
00:02:06,060 --> 00:02:07,750
give it another six
months.

84
00:02:07,750 --> 00:02:09,820
There was nothing left to
give it.

85
00:02:09,820 --> 00:02:10,770
I sat in the parking

86
00:02:10,770 --> 00:02:12,240
lot for a while.

87
00:02:12,240 --> 00:02:13,800
Okay, I thought.

88
00:02:13,800 --> 00:02:15,280
Then explain this.

89
00:02:15,280 --> 00:02:17,410
Anyway, a couple of months
back,

90
00:02:17,410 --> 00:02:18,820
I hit my breaking point.

91
00:02:18,820 --> 00:02:21,020
It was around 2:30 in the
morning.

92
00:02:21,020 --> 00:02:22,080
I'd been on my knees

93
00:02:22,080 --> 00:02:23,950
in somebody's yard all day,

94
00:02:23,950 --> 00:02:26,540
pulling weeds and
spreading mulch.

95
00:02:26,540 --> 00:02:28,290
Everyone in the house was
asleep

96
00:02:28,290 --> 00:02:30,170
and I was downstairs in
the recliner

97
00:02:30,170 --> 00:02:31,210
with my leg up,

98
00:02:31,210 --> 00:02:32,820
trying to find any angle
where

99
00:02:32,820 --> 00:02:33,860
it didn't feel like
something

100
00:02:33,860 --> 00:02:35,060
was wrapped around my knee

101
00:02:35,060 --> 00:02:36,240
and tightening.

102
00:02:36,240 --> 00:02:38,690
My wife didn't know I'd
come downstairs.

103
00:02:38,690 --> 00:02:40,530
By then I'd stopped
telling her.

104
00:02:40,530 --> 00:02:41,220
And I just thought,

105
00:02:41,220 --> 00:02:42,810
is this really my life
now?

106
00:02:42,810 --> 00:02:44,320
I can't live like this.

107
00:02:44,320 --> 00:02:46,130
So I made myself a
promise.

108
00:02:46,130 --> 00:02:46,920
I wouldn't go a day

109
00:02:46,920 --> 00:02:48,620
without looking for an
answer.

110
00:02:48,620 --> 00:02:50,070
And when I found one,

111
00:02:50,070 --> 00:02:51,310
I'd share it with everyone

112
00:02:51,310 --> 00:02:52,920
going through the same
thing.

113
00:02:52,920 --> 00:02:54,010
So I got my laptop

114
00:02:54,010 --> 00:02:55,880
out and went looking.

115
00:02:55,880 --> 00:02:57,150
Not for a product.

116
00:02:57,150 --> 00:02:58,630
For an explanation.

117
00:02:58,630 --> 00:03:00,270
Mayo Clinic forums,

118
00:03:00,270 --> 00:03:02,500
the knee replacement group
on Facebook,

119
00:03:02,500 --> 00:03:05,670
doctor videos, medical
animations.

120
00:03:05,670 --> 00:03:06,500
And that's when I found

121
00:03:06,500 --> 00:03:08,290
a video from a physical
therapist

122
00:03:08,290 --> 00:03:08,930
named Dr.

123
00:03:08,930 --> 00:03:11,310
Steven Salinger, whose own
wife

124
00:03:11,310 --> 00:03:13,290
had been through exactly
this.

125
00:03:13,290 --> 00:03:15,110
But before I say anything
else,

126
00:03:15,110 --> 00:03:16,790
I want to be straight with
you.

127
00:03:16,790 --> 00:03:18,830
You've already had
something work fast.

128
00:03:18,830 --> 00:03:19,570
The ice.

129
00:03:19,570 --> 00:03:21,480
The first week of a new
pill.

130
00:03:21,480 --> 00:03:23,430
The good day after a
session.

131
00:03:23,430 --> 00:03:24,400
Then it wore off.

132
00:03:24,400 --> 00:03:26,690
That's the part nobody
warns you about.

133
00:03:26,690 --> 00:03:28,520
Fast relief isn't relief.

134
00:03:28,520 --> 00:03:29,750
It's a preview.

135
00:03:29,750 --> 00:03:31,110
So I'm not going to tell

136
00:03:31,110 --> 00:03:32,420
you this works fast.

137
00:03:32,420 --> 00:03:33,380
It doesn't.

138
00:03:33,380 --> 00:03:35,380
But if you're willing to
be patient,

139
00:03:35,380 --> 00:03:36,150
and to look at what's

140
00:03:36,150 --> 00:03:37,670
going on around your new
knee

141
00:03:37,670 --> 00:03:39,280
instead of inside it,
there

142
00:03:39,280 --> 00:03:41,570
is a real reason it still
hurts.

143
00:03:41,570 --> 00:03:43,410
And something you can do
about it.

144
00:03:43,410 --> 00:03:44,670
Let me explain what he
said,

145
00:03:44,670 --> 00:03:46,830
because this is what
changed

146
00:03:46,830 --> 00:03:47,970
everything for me.

147
00:03:47,970 --> 00:03:50,320
He started with the
basics.

148
00:03:50,320 --> 00:03:51,820
A knee replacement takes
out

149
00:03:51,820 --> 00:03:53,650
the worn joint surfaces
and puts

150
00:03:53,650 --> 00:03:54,790
in metal and plastic.

151
00:03:54,790 --> 00:03:57,110
That's what stops the
arthritis pain

152
00:03:57,110 --> 00:03:59,120
you had before the
operation.

153
00:03:59,120 --> 00:04:00,830
That part I already knew.

154
00:04:00,830 --> 00:04:02,190
But then he explained
something

155
00:04:02,190 --> 00:04:03,400
nobody had ever told me.

156
00:04:03,400 --> 00:04:04,360
He said,

157
00:04:04,360 --> 00:04:05,830
think about a swollen foot

158
00:04:05,830 --> 00:04:06,960
inside a shoe.

159
00:04:06,960 --> 00:04:08,470
The shoe didn't shrink.

160
00:04:08,470 --> 00:04:10,630
Your foot is taking up
more room,

161
00:04:10,630 --> 00:04:12,130
so everything feels
cramped

162
00:04:12,130 --> 00:04:14,400
and tight and squeezed.

163
00:04:14,400 --> 00:04:15,160
Your new knee sits

164
00:04:15,160 --> 00:04:16,630
in a limited space with
living

165
00:04:16,630 --> 00:04:18,780
tissue packed all around
it.

166
00:04:18,780 --> 00:04:20,600
To put that knee in, the
surgeon

167
00:04:20,600 --> 00:04:22,530
had to work through that
tissue.

168
00:04:22,530 --> 00:04:25,310
Afterwards it gets
inflamed and swollen.

169
00:04:25,310 --> 00:04:27,020
At first that's normal.

170
00:04:27,020 --> 00:04:28,740
But in some people that
swelling can

171
00:04:28,740 --> 00:04:31,670
stay switched on far
longer than expected.

172
00:04:31,670 --> 00:04:33,330
And swollen tissue takes
up more

173
00:04:33,330 --> 00:04:35,220
room than calm tissue
does.

174
00:04:35,220 --> 00:04:36,710
So when you bend,

175
00:04:36,710 --> 00:04:38,590
that tissue gets
compressed.

176
00:04:38,590 --> 00:04:40,020
When you straighten,

177
00:04:40,020 --> 00:04:41,600
it gets pulled tight.

178
00:04:41,600 --> 00:04:42,930
That's the band.

179
00:04:42,930 --> 00:04:45,590
That's the ache that never
quite leaves.

180
00:04:45,590 --> 00:04:46,590
And you start being

181
00:04:46,590 --> 00:04:48,080
the one who says,

182
00:04:48,080 --> 00:04:49,110
you go ahead.

183
00:04:49,110 --> 00:04:50,400
I'll stay here.

184
00:04:50,400 --> 00:04:52,140
And that's exactly why so
much

185
00:04:52,140 --> 00:04:54,430
of what I'd tried hadn't
worked.

186
00:04:54,430 --> 00:04:56,470
Physical therapy
strengthens the muscles

187
00:04:56,470 --> 00:04:57,560
around the knee.

188
00:04:57,560 --> 00:04:58,420
Worth doing,

189
00:04:58,420 --> 00:04:59,570
and I'd done it.

190
00:04:59,570 --> 00:05:01,080
It does nothing about
tissue

191
00:05:01,080 --> 00:05:02,410
taking up room.

192
00:05:02,410 --> 00:05:03,840
A nerve block quiets

193
00:05:03,840 --> 00:05:05,650
the nerve carrying the
signal.

194
00:05:05,650 --> 00:05:08,060
It doesn't touch what's
generating it.

195
00:05:08,060 --> 00:05:09,700
But when that irritated
tissue

196
00:05:09,700 --> 00:05:11,230
finally calms down,

197
00:05:11,230 --> 00:05:12,800
it holds less fluid,

198
00:05:12,800 --> 00:05:14,620
and it takes up less room.

199
00:05:14,620 --> 00:05:15,900
Less room taken up means

200
00:05:15,900 --> 00:05:18,040
less pressure squeezing
the joint.

201
00:05:18,040 --> 00:05:19,920
That's what takes the
pressure off.

202
00:05:19,920 --> 00:05:21,580
After two years of this,

203
00:05:21,580 --> 00:05:22,790
it finally made sense.

204
00:05:22,790 --> 00:05:25,290
The problem was never the
new knee.

205
00:05:25,290 --> 00:05:27,330
It was the tissue crowded
around it.

206
00:05:27,330 --> 00:05:28,980
He calls it the squeeze.

207
00:05:28,980 --> 00:05:31,230
Once you've felt it,
that's the word.

208
00:05:31,230 --> 00:05:32,240
I'd bought knee sleeves,

209
00:05:32,240 --> 00:05:34,160
compression braces,
creams,

210
00:05:34,160 --> 00:05:35,710
half of Amazon really,

211
00:05:35,710 --> 00:05:37,180
and all any of it gave me

212
00:05:37,180 --> 00:05:38,390
was an hour.

213
00:05:38,390 --> 00:05:39,340
I even looked at going

214
00:05:39,340 --> 00:05:41,420
to a clinic for the light
therapy.

215
00:05:41,420 --> 00:05:43,690
But at $200 a session

216
00:05:43,690 --> 00:05:45,510
with nothing covered by
insurance,

217
00:05:45,510 --> 00:05:47,430
that was a quick no.

218
00:05:47,430 --> 00:05:48,510
Then one night I went

219
00:05:48,510 --> 00:05:49,770
back to that knee
replacement

220
00:05:49,770 --> 00:05:51,790
group and actually read
it.

221
00:05:51,790 --> 00:05:53,110
Thousands of people,

222
00:05:53,110 --> 00:05:54,790
years out from surgery,

223
00:05:54,790 --> 00:05:57,200
comparing notes on
stiffness and tightness

224
00:05:57,200 --> 00:05:58,790
nobody could explain.

225
00:05:58,790 --> 00:06:00,570
And no matter how far I
scrolled,

226
00:06:00,570 --> 00:06:02,780
the same thing kept coming
up.

227
00:06:02,780 --> 00:06:04,630
This one device,

228
00:06:04,630 --> 00:06:06,080
and people saying it was
the first

229
00:06:06,080 --> 00:06:07,460
thing that made a
difference.

230
00:06:07,460 --> 00:06:09,390
And before anyone jumps in
thinking,

231
00:06:09,390 --> 00:06:10,880
alright, here it comes,

232
00:06:10,880 --> 00:06:12,570
he's selling me something,

233
00:06:12,570 --> 00:06:14,580
let me shut that down
right now.

234
00:06:14,580 --> 00:06:16,330
I'm only here because I
made myself

235
00:06:16,330 --> 00:06:17,950
a promise at 2:30 in the
morning

236
00:06:17,950 --> 00:06:18,780
that if I ever found

237
00:06:18,780 --> 00:06:19,630
something that helped,

238
00:06:19,630 --> 00:06:20,750
I'd say so.

239
00:06:20,750 --> 00:06:22,400
It's called the KenRelief
Red

240
00:06:22,400 --> 00:06:23,600
Light Therapy Wrap.

241
00:06:23,600 --> 00:06:25,710
At first glance I didn't
buy it.

242
00:06:25,710 --> 00:06:26,810
It looked like the cheap

243
00:06:26,810 --> 00:06:28,210
knee sleeves off Amazon

244
00:06:28,210 --> 00:06:29,900
that did nothing for me.

245
00:06:29,900 --> 00:06:31,920
But I went to their
website anyway,

246
00:06:31,920 --> 00:06:32,800
just to see what all

247
00:06:32,800 --> 00:06:34,270
the fuss was about.

248
00:06:34,270 --> 00:06:36,120
It's the same red light
therapy

249
00:06:36,120 --> 00:06:38,380
clinics charge $200 a
session

250
00:06:38,380 --> 00:06:40,650
for, off machines that
cost

251
00:06:40,650 --> 00:06:42,340
fifty thousand dollars,

252
00:06:42,340 --> 00:06:43,280
in a wrap you plug

253
00:06:43,280 --> 00:06:44,720
into the wall at home.

254
00:06:44,720 --> 00:06:46,770
Two hundred and forty
lights.

255
00:06:46,770 --> 00:06:48,900
Red at 660 nanometers

256
00:06:48,900 --> 00:06:51,470
and near-infrared at 850,

257
00:06:51,470 --> 00:06:53,970
run together for the
strongest effect.

258
00:06:53,970 --> 00:06:55,500
Four strength levels.

259
00:06:55,500 --> 00:06:57,760
A five to thirty minute
timer.

260
00:06:57,760 --> 00:06:59,460
Then I saw the guarantee.

261
00:06:59,460 --> 00:07:00,910
Ninety days.

262
00:07:00,910 --> 00:07:03,190
Results or your money
back,

263
00:07:03,190 --> 00:07:06,040
no questions, no store
credit,

264
00:07:06,040 --> 00:07:08,100
and you don't even send it
back.

265
00:07:08,100 --> 00:07:10,630
No physical therapist ever
gave me ninety

266
00:07:10,630 --> 00:07:12,500
days to change my mind.

267
00:07:12,500 --> 00:07:13,700
There wasn't much to lose,

268
00:07:13,700 --> 00:07:15,410
so I ordered it.

269
00:07:15,410 --> 00:07:16,950
Two of them, actually.

270
00:07:16,950 --> 00:07:18,820
Only the right knee was
replaced,

271
00:07:18,820 --> 00:07:21,170
but you favor the leg that
hurts,

272
00:07:21,170 --> 00:07:23,290
and I'd done it for two
years.

273
00:07:23,290 --> 00:07:25,160
The left one was carrying
the difference.

274
00:07:25,160 --> 00:07:26,110
When it came,

275
00:07:26,110 --> 00:07:28,740
I strapped it on expecting
nothing,

276
00:07:28,740 --> 00:07:30,050
because I'd been let down
too

277
00:07:30,050 --> 00:07:31,790
many times to get excited.

278
00:07:31,790 --> 00:07:33,890
What I felt was warmth.

279
00:07:33,890 --> 00:07:36,220
Not a heating pad kind of
hot.

280
00:07:36,220 --> 00:07:38,110
More like it was coming
from inside

281
00:07:38,110 --> 00:07:40,400
the knee and spreading
around it.

282
00:07:40,400 --> 00:07:41,790
And that was it.

283
00:07:41,790 --> 00:07:43,780
That was the whole
experience.

284
00:07:43,780 --> 00:07:45,030
When I took it off,

285
00:07:45,030 --> 00:07:46,070
I'll be honest,

286
00:07:46,070 --> 00:07:48,220
nothing dramatic had
happened.

287
00:07:48,220 --> 00:07:49,670
And after what that video
said,

288
00:07:49,670 --> 00:07:52,080
that's exactly what I
expected.

289
00:07:52,080 --> 00:07:53,200
What was different

290
00:07:53,200 --> 00:07:54,170
was that for the first

291
00:07:54,170 --> 00:07:55,580
time in two years

292
00:07:55,580 --> 00:07:57,480
I'd done something for my
knee

293
00:07:57,480 --> 00:07:58,840
instead of to it.

294
00:07:58,840 --> 00:08:00,020
Twenty minutes,

295
00:08:00,020 --> 00:08:01,110
in my own chair.

296
00:08:01,110 --> 00:08:03,060
No drive, no copay.

297
00:08:03,060 --> 00:08:04,700
They say twenty minutes.

298
00:08:04,700 --> 00:08:05,740
I did thirty,

299
00:08:05,740 --> 00:08:06,830
twice a day,

300
00:08:06,830 --> 00:08:08,870
lowest setting that first
week.

301
00:08:08,870 --> 00:08:10,240
I put it on the calendar.

302
00:08:10,240 --> 00:08:11,270
The first week,

303
00:08:11,270 --> 00:08:12,140
I couldn't have told

304
00:08:12,140 --> 00:08:13,650
you if anything was
happening.

305
00:08:13,650 --> 00:08:14,550
I tried not to get

306
00:08:14,550 --> 00:08:15,670
my hopes up.

307
00:08:15,670 --> 00:08:17,220
I'd had things help for a
week

308
00:08:17,220 --> 00:08:18,430
and then stop.

309
00:08:18,430 --> 00:08:19,910
But somewhere in the
second week

310
00:08:19,910 --> 00:08:20,970
I noticed I'd come down

311
00:08:20,970 --> 00:08:23,100
the stairs without holding
the rail.

312
00:08:23,100 --> 00:08:24,550
I hadn't decided to.

313
00:08:24,550 --> 00:08:25,630
I just did it,

314
00:08:25,630 --> 00:08:26,920
then stopped halfway down

315
00:08:26,920 --> 00:08:28,570
because I realized.

316
00:08:28,570 --> 00:08:30,150
By the end of the fourth
week

317
00:08:30,150 --> 00:08:31,280
I'd slept through the
night

318
00:08:31,280 --> 00:08:32,750
four times running.

319
00:08:32,750 --> 00:08:33,710
I stood at the counter

320
00:08:33,710 --> 00:08:34,660
and finished making dinner

321
00:08:34,660 --> 00:08:36,310
without looking for the
stool.

322
00:08:36,310 --> 00:08:37,760
None of that is dramatic.

323
00:08:37,760 --> 00:08:38,520
All of it was gone

324
00:08:38,520 --> 00:08:39,860
for two years.

325
00:08:39,860 --> 00:08:41,440
A few weeks later my wife
asked

326
00:08:41,440 --> 00:08:42,280
if I wanted to walk

327
00:08:42,280 --> 00:08:44,230
the long way around the
block.

328
00:08:44,230 --> 00:08:45,180
And for the first time

329
00:08:45,180 --> 00:08:45,890
in two years,

330
00:08:45,890 --> 00:08:47,130
I said yes.

331
00:08:47,130 --> 00:08:48,870
I wanted to understand
why,

332
00:08:48,870 --> 00:08:50,900
so I read the whole thing.

333
00:08:50,900 --> 00:08:52,630
It comes down to four
steps.

334
00:08:52,630 --> 00:08:53,520
One.

335
00:08:53,520 --> 00:08:55,260
The tissue around a new
knee can

336
00:08:55,260 --> 00:08:58,850
stay inflamed long after
surgery is over.

337
00:08:58,850 --> 00:08:59,800
Two.

338
00:08:59,800 --> 00:09:01,800
Inflamed tissue holds
extra fluid,

339
00:09:01,800 --> 00:09:02,750
so it takes up more

340
00:09:02,750 --> 00:09:04,120
room than it should.

341
00:09:04,120 --> 00:09:04,700
Three.

342
00:09:04,700 --> 00:09:06,530
There's only so much room
in there.

343
00:09:06,530 --> 00:09:08,170
Bending compresses it.

344
00:09:08,170 --> 00:09:09,780
Straightening pulls it
tight.

345
00:09:09,780 --> 00:09:11,110
That's the squeeze.

346
00:09:11,110 --> 00:09:11,640
Four.

347
00:09:11,640 --> 00:09:13,160
Red and near-infrared
light have been

348
00:09:13,160 --> 00:09:15,360
studied for calming that
inflammation,

349
00:09:15,360 --> 00:09:16,590
so the swelling and the
pressure

350
00:09:16,590 --> 00:09:18,100
can come down with it.

351
00:09:18,100 --> 00:09:19,120
In a randomized trial,

352
00:09:19,120 --> 00:09:20,890
patients given light
therapy after

353
00:09:20,890 --> 00:09:21,990
a knee replacement

354
00:09:21,990 --> 00:09:23,300
had less pain,

355
00:09:23,300 --> 00:09:24,010
less swelling

356
00:09:24,010 --> 00:09:25,330
and better early movement
than

357
00:09:25,330 --> 00:09:26,520
those who weren't.

358
00:09:26,520 --> 00:09:28,980
A 2025 review said the
same,

359
00:09:28,980 --> 00:09:30,510
and was clear the evidence

360
00:09:30,510 --> 00:09:31,670
is still limited.

361
00:09:31,670 --> 00:09:33,320
I probably sound like a
broken record

362
00:09:33,320 --> 00:09:34,870
to the guys on my crew.

363
00:09:34,870 --> 00:09:36,730
But after two years of
doing everything

364
00:09:36,730 --> 00:09:38,770
I was told and getting
nowhere,

365
00:09:38,770 --> 00:09:40,060
you have no idea what it's

366
00:09:40,060 --> 00:09:41,650
like to sleep through the
night,

367
00:09:41,650 --> 00:09:43,130
say yes to the walk,

368
00:09:43,130 --> 00:09:44,660
and get my life back.

369
00:09:44,660 --> 00:09:46,150
So take it from me.

370
00:09:46,150 --> 00:09:47,590
Don't spend another year
waiting

371
00:09:47,590 --> 00:09:48,670
for it to settle.

372
00:09:48,670 --> 00:09:50,520
Don't spend two hundred a
session.

373
00:09:50,520 --> 00:09:51,820
More than ten thousand
people

374
00:09:51,820 --> 00:09:52,910
with pain after a knee

375
00:09:52,910 --> 00:09:55,010
replacement have already
tried this.

376
00:09:55,010 --> 00:09:56,960
Some had it worse than I
did.

377
00:09:56,960 --> 00:09:58,150
You can get the KenRelief

378
00:09:58,150 --> 00:09:59,900
wrap from their website,

379
00:09:59,900 --> 00:10:01,470
with a discount link

380
00:10:01,470 --> 00:10:03,270
and ninety days to try it.

381
00:10:03,270 --> 00:10:05,320
If it doesn't do anything
for you,

382
00:10:05,320 --> 00:10:06,900
you get your money back

383
00:10:06,900 --> 00:10:08,610
and you keep the wrap.

384
00:10:08,610 --> 00:10:10,160
They only release so many

385
00:10:10,160 --> 00:10:11,490
at that price.

386
00:10:11,490 --> 00:10:12,740
If it's still there,

387
00:10:12,740 --> 00:10:13,500
get one,

388
00:10:13,500 --> 00:10:15,032
and stop the squeeze.
